A lot of Appwrite’s growth has come from developers sharing it with other developers.

Maybe you recommended Appwrite to a teammate, used it in a tutorial, mentioned it in a community thread, or introduced it during a workshop. However it happened, those recommendations have played a huge part in helping more developers discover and build with Appwrite.

That kind of support has meant a lot to us, and we wanted to give something back to the people helping us grow.

Today, we're introducing **Appwrite Affiliates**: create invite links from your Appwrite account, share them however you already share things, and earn **$15 in organization credits to use on Appwrite Cloud** every time someone you refer upgrades to Pro. It's live on [Appwrite Cloud](/affiliates) today.

# What is the Appwrite Affiliates program?

The Appwrite Affiliates program is a referral program for developers. You generate invite links in the Appwrite Console, and when someone signs up through one of your links and later upgrades to [Appwrite Pro](/pricing), you earn $15 in organization credits that you can claim and use on Appwrite Cloud. Clicks, signups, and conversions are tracked for you, and attribution lasts **180 days** after signup.

Here is the whole program in one table.

| Detail              | How it works                                         |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Reward              | $15 in organization credits per referred Pro upgrade |
| Qualifying event    | A referred user upgrades to Appwrite Pro             |
| Attribution window  | 180 days after an attributed signup                  |
| Attribution model   | Last invite link clicked before signup               |
| Where credits land  | Organization credits on Appwrite Cloud               |
| Where you manage it | **Account**, then **Affiliates**, in the Console     |
| Cost to join        | Free, available on Appwrite Cloud                    |

There’s no separate affiliate dashboard to manage. Everything lives in your Appwrite account.

# How to join Appwrite Affiliates in three steps

**1. Create an Appwrite Cloud account.** If you already build on Appwrite, you're done with this step. Affiliates lives in your personal account, not inside a specific project.

**2. Open Affiliates in the Console.** Go to **Account**, then [**Affiliates**](/account/affiliates). This is where links, referrals, rewards, and analytics all live.

**3. Create your first invite link and share it.** Create an invite link for a campaign or channel and share it with your audience. Appwrite tracks visits and attributes signups made through that link.

Create a separate link per channel instead of reusing one everywhere. A link named `youtube-auth-tutorial` and a link named `conf-workshop` cost nothing extra, and they tell you which audience actually converts.

# Track clicks and conversions in the Appwrite Console

Referral programs usually fail on measurement. You share a link, something happens, and a spreadsheet shows up at the end of the month. Appwrite Affiliates reports the same funnel you'd expect from your own product analytics, in the Console you already use.

| Metric      | What it counts                           |
| ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Clicks      | Visits to your invite links              |
| Signups     | New accounts attributed to your links    |
| Conversions | Attributed accounts that upgraded to Pro |

Alongside those totals, the overview shows signup and conversion rates, helping you understand which invite links and channels perform best. 

You can also manage your invite links, referrals, and rewards from the same dashboard, and claim credits when rewards are ready.

Because attribution lasts 180 days, developers have time to try Appwrite before deciding whether to upgrade to Pro.

# How referral rewards and Cloud credits work

When a referred user upgrades to Pro within the 180-day attribution window, you earn $15 in Appwrite Cloud credits. Rewards can be claimed from the Affiliates dashboard.

Claiming asks you to pick an organization you own, and the credits are added there as organization credits that you can use on Appwrite Cloud.

Here’s how the referral journey works:

| Stage | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| Signup | Someone signs up through your invite link and is attributed to you |
| Pro upgrade | They upgrade to Pro within 180 days and you earn a $15 reward |
| No upgrade | If they don’t upgrade within the attribution window, no reward is generated |

Only Pro upgrades generate a reward. Referrals that stay on the Free plan can still appear in your referral analytics as attributed signups.

# Why the 180-day attribution window matters

Short attribution windows don't always reflect how developers choose backend tools. Developers may discover a tool, try it on a project, and only decide to upgrade months later.

The real path looks like this: a developer watches your tutorial, spins up a side project on the Free plan, builds for a couple of months, gets actual users, and then upgrades when limits start to bite. Under a 30-day window, you did all the work and the attribution was gone before the decision happened.

**180 days covers the gap between discovery and the upgrade.** A developer can discover Appwrite, start building on the Free plan, and upgrade later without the referral expiring after only a few weeks.

# Who the Appwrite Affiliates program is for

The program is open to anyone with an Appwrite Cloud account, but it pays off most for people who already recommend tools as part of their work:

* **Creators and educators** publishing tutorials, courses, or videos that use Appwrite for [auth](/products/auth), [databases](/products/databases), or [functions](/products/functions).
* **Agencies and freelancers** who pick the backend for client projects and hand those projects over.
* **Open source maintainers** shipping starters, templates, or boilerplates that developers clone and deploy.
* **Community organizers** running workshops, hackathons, and meetups where attendees build something real.

One honest caveat: rewards depend on Cloud Pro upgrades. If your audience self-hosts Appwrite, which is free and open source, you'll see signups without conversions. The same is true of audiences that build purely on the Free plan. Treat Affiliates as credits that offset your own Appwrite bill for work you're already doing, not as a revenue line. If your situation is different, our [Startups](/startups) and [Education](/education) programs may fit better.

# Getting started with Appwrite Affiliates

Appwrite Affiliates is available on Appwrite Cloud today. Open [Account, then Affiliates](/account/affiliates), create your first invite link, share Appwrite the way you already do, and start earning credits when the developers you refer upgrade to Pro.

We’re excited to finally give something back to the people who have helped Appwrite grow, and we can’t wait to see where you share it next.

